{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review & compensate graduates whose student debt is higher than amount borrowed",
        "additional_details": "We want the Government to launch an independent review into this phenomenon and whether student loans were mis-sold. The review should also look into ways to improve transparency so future students fully understand the long-term cost of borrowing.\r\n \r\nThe Government should fund writing off debt above the original amount borrowed for long-term borrowers who have consistently repaid and compensate those who have been found to be financially disadvantaged by inflation-linked interest. We believe borrowers who have responsibly repaid their loans for years should not find themselves owing more than they originally borrowed.",
        "background": "Thousands of students were unaware that inflation-linked interest could increase their loan balance despite years of repayments. Many graduates now owe more than they originally borrowed for their student loans.",
